ation interface, collect user inputs, and maintain the operational logs required to run distributional sampling and drift-keyed re-measurement on live outputs. Congress established this precise division of responsibility in Section 230 of the Communications Decency Act, recognizing that the infrastructure provider cannot police the infinite downstream applications built upon its substrate. State legislatures should reject upstream strict liability statutes and instead enforce strict operational standards at the deployer boundary where actual harm prevention is technically feasible.",
